{"question_id": "q03-terrain-slope", "run": 1, "cache": "cold", "status": "ok", "error": null, "latency_s": 15.96, "provenance": {"at": "2026-10-19T23:37:42.918Z", "turn_id": "turn_c53550a9", "session_id": "b709f6588aa3", "subject": "anonymous", "model": "eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5", "models_used": ["eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5"], "prompt_version": "a9f7e88fc432", "memory_context": false, "sdk": "pydantic-ai-slim 2.54.0", "tools_called": ["geocode", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation", "render_object"], "num_turns": 5, "duration_ms": 15686, "duration_api_ms": null, "total_cost_usd": 0.02528823, "usage": {"input_tokens": 12, "output_tokens": 1343, "cache_read_input_tokens": 42328, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2121}, "is_error": false, "retried_fresh": false, "refused": false, "error": null, "http_status": null, "runtime": "pydantic-ai", "provider": "bedrock", "cost_source": "genai-prices 0.1.13 (regional.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5)"}, "images": 1, "files": 0, "answer": "I analyzed the terrain in a 600 m \u00d7 600 m area centered on Chalmers (EPSG:3006 bounds 319200, 6397700, 319800, 6398300). I used 412,446 ground-classified points to build a 2 m DEM, then computed slope and aspect from it.\n\n**Elevation**\n- Elevation runs from 41.3 m to 87.1 m, about 46 m of relief across the area.\n- The mean is 61.5 m and the median is 61.9 m.\n- The 5th to 95th percentile range is 46.5 m to 75.0 m.\n\n**Slope**\nThe tool doesn't state units. I assumed radians because the aspect values span \u00b1\u03c0, so the degree figures below rest on that assumption.\n\n| Statistic | Radians | Degrees |\n|---|---|---|\n| Min | 0.00 | 0\u00b0 |\n| Median | 0.074 | about 4.2\u00b0 |\n| Mean | 0.154 | about 8.8\u00b0 |\n| 95th percentile | 0.553 | about 31.7\u00b0 |\n| Max | 1.291 | about 74\u00b0 |\n\n- **Overall:** Most of the area is gentle. Half the cells are under about 4\u00b0.\n- **Steep cells:** The top 5% of cells are steeper than about 32\u00b0. The maximum is about 74\u00b0, which probably comes from rock outcrops or cuts and embankments.\n- **Aspect:** It ranges over the full \u2212\u03c0 to \u03c0, with a mean near 0 and a median of about \u22120.2 rad. The aspect statistics don't show a dominant facing direction.\n\n**Visualization**\nI rendered a 3D terrain mesh of the area (8,490 triangles, 10 m mesh size). It shows the terrain shape only, not a slope field. The slope and aspect results are summary statistics with no locations, so I can't say where the steep or flat areas are.\n\nI can export the slope raster, or rerun at a finer cell size or over a different area, if you'd like.", "operations": [{"at": "2026-10-19T23:37:28.720Z", "turn_id": "turn_c53550a9", "session_id": "b709f6588aa3", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "geocode", "operation": null, "params_hash": "ad5faefbe482eb39", "seconds": 0.002, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": [], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:37:32.082Z", "turn_id": "turn_c53550a9", "session_id": "b709f6588aa3", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "60eb5c049e03b34b", "seconds": 2.033, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["obj_e38a56eb"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:37:33.904Z", "turn_id": "turn_c53550a9", "session_id": "b709f6588aa3", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "builder.build_terrain_raster", "params_hash": "8b5d36e5482c3839", "seconds": 0.114, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["obj_e990d109"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:37:34.067Z", "turn_id": "turn_c53550a9", "session_id": "b709f6588aa3", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "builder.build_terrain_surface_mesh", "params_hash": "bac88c9d61111212", "seconds": 0.276, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["obj_d3c21a91"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:37:35.966Z", "turn_id": "turn_c53550a9", "session_id": "b709f6588aa3", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "render_object", "operation": null, "params_hash": "5746e2392879a782", "seconds": 0.72, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["obj_d3c21a91"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:37:36.292Z", "turn_id": "turn_c53550a9", "session_id": "b709f6588aa3", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "builder.raster.slope_aspect", "params_hash": "4d5f4b6525b7d69f", "seconds": 1.045, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["obj_cce1cc4f", "obj_9dece4a6"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}
{"question_id": "q09-too-large", "run": 1, "cache": "cold", "status": "ok", "error": null, "latency_s": 16.92, "provenance": {"at": "2026-10-19T23:37:59.838Z", "turn_id": "turn_538f52ac", "session_id": "2349d4a091bb", "subject": "anonymous", "model": "eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5", "models_used": ["eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5"], "prompt_version": "a9f7e88fc432", "memory_context": false, "sdk": "pydantic-ai-slim 2.54.0", "tools_called": ["geocode", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation"], "num_turns": 4, "duration_ms": 16497, "duration_api_ms": null, "total_cost_usd": 0.03286019, "usage": {"input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 1859, "cache_read_input_tokens": 33179, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3178}, "is_error": false, "retried_fresh": false, "refused": false, "error": null, "http_status": null, "runtime": "pydantic-ai", "provider": "bedrock", "cost_source": "genai-prices 0.1.13 (regional.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5)"}, "images": 0, "files": 0, "answer": "I got the point cloud for central Gothenburg. A single 5 \u00d7 5 km download (25 km\u00b2) was refused because the limit is 10 km\u00b2 per download. I split the area into four 2.5 \u00d7 2.5 km tiles, and all four loaded.\n\nThe geocoder only returned a small box around G\u00f6teborg Central station, so I built the area myself. It is centred on the station (E 319676, N 6400380 in EPSG:3006) and covers x 317176\u2013322176 and y 6397880\u20136402880.\n\n| Tile | Object ref | Points | Elevation range (m) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| SW | `obj_233dc5b9` | 12.61 M | \u2212133 to 115 |\n| SE | `obj_262d5a07` | 13.99 M | \u221297 to 568 |\n| NW | `obj_368335c3` | 10.80 M | \u2212228 to 314 |\n| NE | `obj_3b5779db` | 10.37 M | \u2212334 to 503 |\n\nIn total that is about **47.8 million points**. Each tile includes these classes:\n- **Unclassified (1) and ground (2):** these make up most of the points in every tile.\n- **Building (9):** the SW tile has about 686,000 points, and the other tiles have under 30,000 each.\n- **Other classes:** low points (7), water (17) and bridge/other (18) are also present.\n\nThe minimum and maximum elevations in the table look like noise rather than real terrain. Examples are \u2212334 m and 568 m, in a city that is close to sea level. You can remove the outliers by downloading with `remove_outliers: true`.\n\nThe four tiles are separate objects and I haven't merged them. I can build a terrain mesh or DEM per tile, filter to ground or buildings, or export them.", "operations": [{"at": "2026-10-19T23:37:45.266Z", "turn_id": "turn_538f52ac", "session_id": "2349d4a091bb", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "geocode", "operation": null, "params_hash": "862c813d77e68dca", "seconds": 0.133, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": [], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:37:47.596Z", "turn_id": "turn_538f52ac", "session_id": "2349d4a091bb", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "4d1fe6a0fec4fdb2", "seconds": 0.001, "ok": false, "error": "Refused", "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": [], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:37:53.968Z", "turn_id": "turn_538f52ac", "session_id": "2349d4a091bb", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "86d956ceacb1e445", "seconds": 0.953, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": true, "object_refs": ["obj_233dc5b9"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:37:54.083Z", "turn_id": "turn_538f52ac", "session_id": "2349d4a091bb", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "283de0b0553533c7", "seconds": 1.067, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": true, "object_refs": ["obj_262d5a07"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:37:54.767Z", "turn_id": "turn_538f52ac", "session_id": "2349d4a091bb", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "92875b6c0fb1314e", "seconds": 1.748, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": true, "object_refs": ["obj_368335c3"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:37:54.801Z", "turn_id": "turn_538f52ac", "session_id": "2349d4a091bb", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "e9a155852398175c", "seconds": 1.782, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": true, "object_refs": ["obj_3b5779db"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}
{"question_id": "q03-terrain-slope", "run": 2, "cache": "warm", "status": "ok", "error": null, "latency_s": 13.88, "provenance": {"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:13.727Z", "turn_id": "turn_8821b412", "session_id": "9e8ae4eb13b4", "subject": "anonymous", "model": "eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5", "models_used": ["eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5"], "prompt_version": "a9f7e88fc432", "memory_context": false, "sdk": "pydantic-ai-slim 2.54.0", "tools_called": ["geocode", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation", "render_object"], "num_turns": 6, "duration_ms": 13688, "duration_api_ms": null, "total_cost_usd": 0.02658601, "usage": {"input_tokens": 14, "output_tokens": 1368, "cache_read_input_tokens": 52111, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2100}, "is_error": false, "retried_fresh": false, "refused": false, "error": null, "http_status": null, "runtime": "pydantic-ai", "provider": "bedrock", "cost_source": "genai-prices 0.1.13 (regional.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5)"}, "images": 1, "files": 0, "answer": "I analysed a 600 \u00d7 600 m area around Chalmers (EPSG:3006: 319200\u2013319800 E, 6397700\u20136398300 N). I used 412,446 ground-classified lidar points to build a 2 m DEM, then computed slope and aspect from it.\n\n**Elevation**\n- Elevation runs from 41.4 m to 86.9 m, a relief of about 45 m.\n- The mean is 61.4 m and the median is 62.2 m.\n- The 5th to 95th percentile range is 46.5 to 75.0 m.\n\n**Slope**\n\nThe tool doesn't label the slope unit. I assumed radians, since the aspect raster is clearly in radians (\u2212\u03c0 to \u03c0). The degree values are my conversion.\n\n| Statistic | Radians | Degrees |\n|---|---|---|\n| Median | 0.074 | ~4.2\u00b0 |\n| Mean | 0.154 | ~8.8\u00b0 |\n| 95th percentile | 0.553 | ~31.7\u00b0 |\n| Max | 1.291 | ~74\u00b0 |\n\n- **Overall terrain:** Most of the area is gentle. Half the cells are under about 4\u00b0 and the mean is about 9\u00b0.\n- **Steep areas:** The top 5% of cells are steeper than about 32\u00b0. Some cells reach about 74\u00b0, which suggests steep rock outcrops or cut slopes. Isolated steep cells can also come from DEM artifacts, such as gaps where buildings were removed from the ground points.\n- **Aspect:** The aspect values span the full circle, with a mean near 0 and a standard deviation of about 1.75 rad. No single slope direction dominates.\n\n**Visualization**\n\nI rendered a 3D terrain mesh of the area. It shows the terrain shape only, not a slope overlay. The slope and aspect summaries have no spatial breakdown, so I can't say which parts of campus are steep or flat.\n\nThe raster references are `obj_f8b97eff` (slope) and `obj_ec188b92` (aspect). I can export them, or repeat the analysis with a finer cell size or a smaller area.", "operations": [{"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:01.200Z", "turn_id": "turn_8821b412", "session_id": "9e8ae4eb13b4", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "geocode", "operation": null, "params_hash": "ad5faefbe482eb39", "seconds": 0.001, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": [], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:02.533Z", "turn_id": "turn_8821b412", "session_id": "9e8ae4eb13b4", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "60eb5c049e03b34b", "seconds": 0.041, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": true, "object_refs": ["obj_c1eb9fc2"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:03.845Z", "turn_id": "turn_8821b412", "session_id": "9e8ae4eb13b4", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "builder.build_terrain_raster", "params_hash": "6d3cfd0aeee7ab06", "seconds": 0.066, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["obj_9c4e3f26"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:05.537Z", "turn_id": "turn_8821b412", "session_id": "9e8ae4eb13b4", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "builder.raster.slope_aspect", "params_hash": "28c6597d9048391f", "seconds": 0.025, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["obj_f8b97eff", "obj_ec188b92"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:05.681Z", "turn_id": "turn_8821b412", "session_id": "9e8ae4eb13b4", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "builder.build_terrain_surface_mesh", "params_hash": "d178f5d208fc4fd2", "seconds": 0.167, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["obj_65ee0b76"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:06.942Z", "turn_id": "turn_8821b412", "session_id": "9e8ae4eb13b4", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "render_object", "operation": null, "params_hash": "1061356610de05ad", "seconds": 0.11, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["obj_65ee0b76"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}
{"question_id": "q09-too-large", "run": 2, "cache": "warm", "status": "ok", "error": null, "latency_s": 18.06, "provenance": {"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:31.789Z", "turn_id": "turn_7b74733a", "session_id": "35d096588dd7", "subject": "anonymous", "model": "eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5", "models_used": ["eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5"], "prompt_version": "a9f7e88fc432", "memory_context": false, "sdk": "pydantic-ai-slim 2.54.0", "tools_called": ["geocode", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation"], "num_turns": 4, "duration_ms": 17811, "duration_api_ms": null, "total_cost_usd": 0.03481852, "usage": {"input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 2037, "cache_read_input_tokens": 33157, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3179}, "is_error": false, "retried_fresh": false, "refused": false, "error": null, "http_status": null, "runtime": "pydantic-ai", "provider": "bedrock", "cost_source": "genai-prices 0.1.13 (regional.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5)"}, "images": 0, "files": 0, "answer": "I got the point cloud for a 5 \u00d7 5 km area around G\u00f6teborgs central station. The tool wouldn't download it as one 25 km\u00b2 block because it caps a download at 10 km\u00b2. I split it into four 2.5 km tiles (6.25 km\u00b2 each) and all four loaded. The tiles are separate objects, not one merged cloud.\n\n| Tile | Object ref | Points |\n|---|---|---|\n| SW | `obj_ea521f05` | 12.61 M |\n| SE | `obj_3ee7dbdc` | 13.99 M |\n| NW | `obj_16033682` | 10.80 M |\n| NE | `obj_86a22913` | 10.37 M |\n| **Total** | | **\u224847.8 M** |\n\n- **Area:** the bounds are EPSG:3006, x 317176\u2013322176 and y 6397880\u20136402880. The geocoder only returned a small box for \"Central Gothenburg\" (about 0.65 \u00d7 1.1 km), so I centred a 5 km box on its centre point at (319676, 6400380).\n- **Classifications:** the tiles hold ground (class 2), unclassified (class 1), buildings (class 9), water (class 17) and a small amount of noise (classes 7 and 18). Class 9 is mostly in the SW tile (686 k points). The other tiles have only about 19\u201326 k. I don't know why.\n- **Elevation outliers:** the tiles include noise, with z ranging from \u2212334 m to +568 m. The median is about 7\u201329 m, depending on the tile. I'd filter the noise before building terrain or meshes.\n\nI haven't rendered anything, because 48 M points is too heavy to draw usefully. If you want a visual, I can render a terrain mesh for one tile or a smaller sub-area. I can also filter to ground only or building points.", "operations": [{"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:15.533Z", "turn_id": "turn_7b74733a", "session_id": "35d096588dd7", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "geocode", "operation": null, "params_hash": "862c813d77e68dca", "seconds": 0.087, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": [], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:18.356Z", "turn_id": "turn_7b74733a", "session_id": "35d096588dd7", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "fd420760f0e51296", "seconds": 0.001, "ok": false, "error": "Refused", "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": [], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:24.861Z", "turn_id": "turn_7b74733a", "session_id": "35d096588dd7", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "25331dcadaf3148e", "seconds": 0.89, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": true, "object_refs": ["obj_ea521f05"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:24.967Z", "turn_id": "turn_7b74733a", "session_id": "35d096588dd7", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "6671c60720c20d55", "seconds": 0.994, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": true, "object_refs": ["obj_3ee7dbdc"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:25.455Z", "turn_id": "turn_7b74733a", "session_id": "35d096588dd7", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "3e8cf5bf587343db", "seconds": 1.481, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": true, "object_refs": ["obj_16033682"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:25.500Z", "turn_id": "turn_7b74733a", "session_id": "35d096588dd7", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "1119043632a4692f", "seconds": 1.526, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": true, "object_refs": ["obj_86a22913"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}
{"question_id": "q03-terrain-slope", "run": 3, "cache": "warm", "status": "ok", "error": null, "latency_s": 12.82, "provenance": {"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:44.613Z", "turn_id": "turn_95657135", "session_id": "cfbfd2d2e824", "subject": "anonymous", "model": "eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5", "models_used": ["eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5"], "prompt_version": "a9f7e88fc432", "memory_context": false, "sdk": "pydantic-ai-slim 2.54.0", "tools_called": ["geocode", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation", "render_object"], "num_turns": 6, "duration_ms": 12564, "duration_api_ms": null, "total_cost_usd": 0.02535775, "usage": {"input_tokens": 14, "output_tokens": 1259, "cache_read_input_tokens": 52095, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2090}, "is_error": false, "retried_fresh": false, "refused": false, "error": null, "http_status": null, "runtime": "pydantic-ai", "provider": "bedrock", "cost_source": "genai-prices 0.1.13 (regional.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5)"}, "images": 1, "files": 0, "answer": "I analyzed the terrain in a 600 \u00d7 600 m area centered on Chalmers (EPSG:3006 bounds 319200\u2013319800 E, 6397700\u20136398300 N). I built a 2 m DEM from 412,446 ground-classified lidar points and computed slope from it.\n\n**Elevation**\n- The range is 41.4\u201386.9 m, a relief of about 45 m.\n- The mean is 61.4 m and the median is 62.2 m.\n- 90% of the area lies between 46.5 and 75.0 m.\n\n**Slope**\n\nThe slope raster has no unit label. I assumed radians, because the aspect raster spans \u00b1\u03c0. The degree values are my conversion.\n\n| Statistic | Radians | Degrees |\n|---|---|---|\n| Mean | 0.154 | about 8.8\u00b0 |\n| Median | 0.074 | about 4.2\u00b0 |\n| 95th percentile | 0.553 | about 31.7\u00b0 |\n| Max | 1.291 | about 74\u00b0 |\n\n- **Mostly gentle:** The median slope is about 4\u00b0, so most of the area is nearly flat.\n- **Some steep ground:** The 95th percentile is about 32\u00b0 and the maximum is about 74\u00b0. The steepest cells are probably rock outcrops or cut slopes. The area also has a lot of relief, so the slope is uneven. I can't confirm where these cells are, because the statistics have no locations.\n- **Aspect:** Aspect covers the full \u00b1\u03c0 range with a mean near 0, so there is no single dominant slope direction in the summary.\n\nI rendered a 3D terrain mesh (8,490 faces, 10 m mesh size). It shows the terrain shape only. The slope values are not drawn on it, so it doesn't show where the steep areas are.\n\nI can run the same analysis on a smaller sub-area, or add buildings to the view.", "operations": [{"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:33.148Z", "turn_id": "turn_95657135", "session_id": "cfbfd2d2e824", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "geocode", "operation": null, "params_hash": "ad5faefbe482eb39", "seconds": 0.0, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": [], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:34.331Z", "turn_id": "turn_95657135", "session_id": "cfbfd2d2e824", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "60eb5c049e03b34b", "seconds": 0.028, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": true, "object_refs": ["obj_c53e5b60"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:35.361Z", "turn_id": "turn_95657135", "session_id": "cfbfd2d2e824", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "builder.build_terrain_raster", "params_hash": "0201955c12d4825e", "seconds": 0.062, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["obj_727e45b5"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:37.212Z", "turn_id": "turn_95657135", "session_id": "cfbfd2d2e824", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "builder.raster.slope_aspect", "params_hash": "6267b68bf4832e34", "seconds": 0.044, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["obj_b6c95a2b", "obj_d2d2035e"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:37.331Z", "turn_id": "turn_95657135", "session_id": "cfbfd2d2e824", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "builder.build_terrain_surface_mesh", "params_hash": "b442bab598c9d8d8", "seconds": 0.162, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["obj_17cd07b6"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:38.672Z", "turn_id": "turn_95657135", "session_id": "cfbfd2d2e824", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "render_object", "operation": null, "params_hash": "452fe455b5151fe5", "seconds": 0.281, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["obj_17cd07b6"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}
{"question_id": "q09-too-large", "run": 3, "cache": "warm", "status": "ok", "error": null, "latency_s": 10.61, "provenance": {"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:55.221Z", "turn_id": "turn_603863a0", "session_id": "3d5852d07dcd", "subject": "anonymous", "model": "eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5", "models_used": ["eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5"], "prompt_version": "a9f7e88fc432", "memory_context": false, "sdk": "pydantic-ai-slim 2.54.0", "tools_called": ["geocode", "run_operation"], "num_turns": 3, "duration_ms": 10259, "duration_api_ms": null, "total_cost_usd": 0.01471349, "usage": {"input_tokens": 8, "output_tokens": 905, "cache_read_input_tokens": 24399, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 748}, "is_error": false, "retried_fresh": false, "refused": false, "error": null, "http_status": null, "runtime": "pydantic-ai", "provider": "bedrock", "cost_source": "genai-prices 0.1.13 (regional.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5)"}, "images": 0, "files": 0, "answer": "I couldn't download that. A 5 km \u00d7 5 km box is 25 km\u00b2, and one download can cover at most 10 km\u00b2. Larger requests need several GB of memory.\n\nThe geocoder put the centre of \"Central Gothenburg\" at G\u00f6teborgs central station (about E 319676, N 6400380). The 5 km box would run from E 317176 to 322176 and N 6397880 to 6402880.\n\nYou have two options:\n\n1. **One 3 km \u00d7 3 km download (9 km\u00b2).** This is centred on the station and covers the core of the city centre. It is the quickest option.\n2. **Tiles that together cover the 5 km area.** I'd split it into 3 \u00d7 3 tiles of about 1.7 km (2.8 km\u00b2 each), or 4 tiles of 2.5 km (6.25 km\u00b2 each). I'd download each tile separately. They stay separate objects, and I can't merge them into one point cloud. Downloading all of them will take a while.\n\nWhich would you like? If you'd rather I just pick one, I'll do option 1.", "operations": [{"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:47.092Z", "turn_id": "turn_603863a0", "session_id": "3d5852d07dcd", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "geocode", "operation": null, "params_hash": "862c813d77e68dca", "seconds": 0.071, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": [], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:38:49.317Z", "turn_id": "turn_603863a0", "session_id": "3d5852d07dcd", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "fd420760f0e51296", "seconds": 0.001, "ok": false, "error": "Refused", "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": [], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}
